    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95642.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Some people have expressed a view that regenerative agriculture is in a way a distraction from other efforts that need to be taken to help address climate change. And I'm sure you feel the view of soil for climate, which is that Combating emissions is absolutely crucial, but it's not good enough. We also need to get the excess carbon out of the atmosphere back in 2013. The intergovernmental panel on climate change said specifically that we would be facing centuries of warming unless the only exception they gave was if we could draw it out a massive amount of carbon out of the atmosphere and in so doing restoring our ecosystems. So, okay, I'm glad we're on the same",
