  {
    "episode_id": 95642,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95642.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 17,
    "turn_text": "I mean, that's a sign of the times. I mean, this is what I'm trying to do to get rid of it. I keep saying it's not left or right now. It's new and better. Like, how do we get out of this left or right? So here's another perfect example of, well, it's got to be either or it's either, you know, you reduce emissions or you do the soil piece where you're sequestering carbon. It's like, no, who lives in that kind of world? It's so black and white. It's both and new and better. And if we have an initiative where we're capturing carbon, we're building electric vehicles, we're building batteries, we're building charging stations, we're building solar, we're building wind turbines. And capturing carbon, helping our farmers And so it's whole foods for education. We should educate the whole child or the economy. We should make sure that it's a holistic approach concerning stakeholders, not just shareholders, which means workers in the environment. So everything, I think new and better means holistic approach and getting to the root cause of the process.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
